course: dictionary
lesson: 10262
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists them as numbered senses, and the sentence around the word tells you which one is meant. The word tool is a good example: its first meaning is an object you hold to do a job, like a hammer or a spade.
explain: «Counting is one of a scientist's best tools.» Here a tool is not something you hold. It is anything that helps you do something, such as a method. Ask: would the sentence still make sense if I swapped in "method"? If it does, you have found the right meaning.
explain: «Not the sharpest tool in the shed» is an informal phrase. It does not mean a blunt blade. Here a tool means a silly person, and the whole phrase means not clever. The words "dim" and "no Einstein" mean something similar, so the context shows you the meaning and the tone.
fact: A tool is an object you hold and use to do a job, like a hammer, saw, screwdriver or spade.
fact: A tool can also be anything that helps you do something, like a computer program or a method.
fact: «Some of their stone tools are about 3,000 years old.» Here tool means an object, made from stone, that was used to do a job.
fact: In design and technology, tools must be used with care and with an adult: hold them correctly and keep the blades away from you.
fact: Calling someone a tool is informal and a little rude, because it means they are silly or unpleasant.
exercise: What does tool mean in «Counting is one of a scientist's best tools»? | A silly person | A spade for digging | A hammer for nails | *A method that helps you do something
exercise: «Not the sharpest tool in the shed» means what? | Very sharp and dangerous | Good at building sheds | *Not clever | Very tired after work
exercise: Which of these is an object you hold to do a job? | Kindness | *A screwdriver | Bedtime | Happiness
test: «The bathroom has its own good habits: hot hair tools switched off.» What are hot hair tools? | A kind of shampoo | Hair that has gone cold | Brushes made of wood | *Objects, like straighteners, used to style hair
test: Which sentence uses tool to mean a silly person? | "A ruler is a useful tool in maths." | "Pass me the tool so I can fix the chair." | *"He is such a tool, always showing off for nothing." | "This computer tool helps me spell."
exam: In «Wild capuchin monkeys crack hard nuts with stones, and some of their stone tools are about 3,000 years old», what does tool mean? | A rule for playing games | A kind of monkey | Silly person | *An object used to do a job
